  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordination and support to Fish for Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordination of and support to the Fish for Development Programme. The work of the Norwegian Veterinary Institute and the framework agreement on fish health and biosecurity contributes to biodiversity and environmental protection by preventing and controlling fish diseases, reducing the need for medication, and limiting the spread of pathogens and invasive species that can harm wild fish stocks and marine ecosystems. Their research, surveillance and risk assessments also strengthen scientific knowledge and climate adaptation by improving understanding of how climate change affects fish health, guiding more resilient aquaculture practices, and supporting policies that safeguard both farmed and wild aquatic populations.</narrative>
  </description>
